~~ The three unusual things about Bija, in one program.

~~ 1. A seed is a stack of generations. Nothing is overwritten.
"draft" => sow doc.
doc + " revised" => doc.
doc + " again" => doc.

utter doc.        ~~ draft revised again
utter doc@1.      ~~ draft revised
utter doc@2.      ~~ draft
utter depth doc.  ~~ 3

~~ 2. A block can be undone. Output is not.
attempt:
  "ruined" => doc.
  utter "inside the attempt, doc is: " + doc.
  wither.
end.
utter "after the wither, doc is: " + doc.
utter "and its history is still " + text(depth doc) + " deep".

~~ 3. An effect can wait for its conditions to ripen.
0 => sow balance.
ripen when balance >= 100:
  utter "balance reached " + text(balance) + " after " + text(depth balance - 1) + " deposits".
end.

each deposit in [30, 40, 50]:
  balance + deposit => balance.
end.

utter "final balance " + text(balance).
